---
description: Sanitize generated UI artifacts before integrating presentation code
alwaysApply: true
---

When generated or pasted HTML, JSX, or TSX will be integrated:

- First inspect the target component's existing props, state, handlers, routes,
  data flow, and supported product capabilities.
- Invoke `clean_design_artifact` with the untouched artifact, intended component
  name, and an explicit `allowed_features` list.
- If sanitization fails, stop. Never substitute original or partial model output.
- Treat sanitized code as presentation-only. Reconnect existing application logic
  manually; never overwrite, duplicate, or fabricate business logic.
- Reject additions of state, effects, mock data, fake statuses, inline event
  logic, dependencies, routes, controls, or features outside the allowlist.
- Review the diff and run relevant type checks and tests before proposing merge.
